        "original_id": "c686a57b-e650-597c-85c0-c1bb933576c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Pravda, Communist Party of the Soviet Union, Comintern\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Francesco Maria Piave, Lajos Magyar\n- Products: Stiffelio\n- Topics: Russian newspapers, opera, prisoner exchanges\n\nFacts:\n- In 1922, Lajos Magyar went to the Soviet Union as the result of a prisoner exchange.\n- In 1922, Lajos Magyar worked on the staff of the Comintern in the Soviet Union.\n- In 1922, Lajos Magyar worked at the newspaper Pravda in the Soviet Union.\n- Pravda is a Russian broadsheet newspaper.\n- Pravda was formerly the official newspaper of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union.\n- Pravda was once one of the most influential newspapers in the Soviet Union and had a circulation of 11 million.\n- Stiffelio is an opera in three acts by Giuseppe Verdi.\n- The libretto for Stiffelio was written in Italian by Francesco Maria Piave.",
